  },
  "Solution": {
    "S": "Let $X$ be the number of queens drawn. Then $X = 0, 1, 2$.\n\n$$P(X = 0) = \\frac{\\binom{48}{2}}{\\binom{52}{2}} = \\frac{48 \\times 47}{52 \\times 51} = \\frac{188}{221}$$\n\n$$P(X = 1) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{1} \\times \\binom{48}{1}}{\\binom{52}{2}} = \\frac{4 \\times 48}{1326} = \\frac{192}{1326} = \\frac{32}{221}$$\n\n$$P(X = 2) = \\frac{\\binom{4}{2}}{\\binom{52}{2}} = \\frac{6}{1326} = \\frac{1}{221}$$\n\nNow,\n\n$$E(X) = 0 \\times \\frac{188}{221} + 1 \\times \\frac{32}{221} + 2 \\times \\frac{1}{221} = \\frac{32 + 2}{221} = \\frac{34}{221}$$\n\n$$E(X^2) = 0^2 \\times \\frac{188}{221} + 1^2 \\times \\frac{32}{221} + 2^2 \\times \\frac{1}{221} = \\frac{32 + 4}{221} = \\frac{36}{221}$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$2E(X) + 3E(X^2) = 2 \\times \\frac{34}{221} + 3 \\times \\frac{36}{221} = \\frac{68 + 108}{221} = \\frac{176}{221}$$\n\nThus the correct option is C: $\\frac{176}{221}$."
  },
